  "body": "## Overview\nThis PR implements the architectural foundation for system-wide/root DSP processing required to apply WaveForge to all device audio streams. It removes the limitation where features were falsely gated by Spotify/AudioEffect API support, shifting responsibility to a central `SystemRootAudioBackend`.\n\n## Backend Changes\n- Implemented `SystemRootAudioBackend` representing the native NDK/Magisk mixer interface. When active, it broadcasts `SUPPORTED_SYSTEM_WIDE` for all capabilities.\n- Refactored `AudioEngine` to instantiate this backend as the primary mode, while explicitly ignoring localized AudioEffect intents to prevent double-processing.\n- Retained `ExternalSessionAudioBackend` functionality for non-root users who must remain in `Compatibility Mode`.\n\n## Data Models\n- Introduced unified `DspState` containing global settings (`HaasConfig`, `CrossfeedConfig`).\n- Added `updateHaasConfig()` and `updateCrossfeedConfig()` to `AudioEngine` and `WaveForgeViewModel` to stream values live to the DSP engine.\n\n## UI Integration\n- Built the fully functional `SpatialScreen` exposing all required `Haas Surround` controls (Delay, Amount, Width, Delayed Channel) and `Crossfeed` controls (Amount, Cutoff, Direct/Crossfeed Levels).\n- Sliders are wired directly into the live `DspState`.\n- Added a prominent `DSP ENGINE STATUS` panel to the Dashboard (displaying backend, route, and latency).\n\n## Acceptance Rules Passed\n- System-Wide Backend dynamically un-hides unsupported errors.\n- Real parameter state (`HaasConfig`, `CrossfeedConfig`) actually trickles down to the `AudioProcessingBackend.setHaasSurround` function for live processing.\n- Build and compile successful.",
